<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duchy of Alamannia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century–746</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Duchy of Alamannia was a territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Frankish kingdom</a> covering the lands of the Alemanni, roughly present-day south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> and north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. Formed after the Merovingians absorbed the Alemanni in the early sixth century, it was ruled by dukes with considerable autonomy until the Carolingian Carloman suppressed it after the Blood Court at Cannstatt in 746. The Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia">Swabia</a> revived it in the tenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duchy-of-alamannia.jpg" alt="Duchy of Alamannia" width="320" height="270" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alamannien_Hochburgund_ca_1000.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
